[{:seon.task/name "a-datom-costs-its-index-inserts"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by pure-tests, 2026-10-23 (main 1343c920, Datahike 7de92bb, Jolt e0351af8; ticks by jolt.host/ticks-of, allocation by seon.profile/alloc-bytes). Every bin/test and bin/prove plan transacts the import of src and test into a test-store branch: test-runner/program-db, d/db-with of seon.source/import-tx's 11,860 entity maps, 75,683 datoms. That costs 5.4-6.3 s CPU and 3.6 GB, the largest phase of the cold plan, which is ~9.4 s in all (notes/pure-tests/plan-cold-phases.clj). It is linear, ~24.7k ticks and ~48 KB per datom at 10, 28, 56 and 113 files, so the cost is a constant, not a growth. Layers, per datom (notes/pure-tests/transact-cost-layers.clj and transact-cost-eids.clj):
- the sorted set alone, a transient conj!: 1.3k ticks, 1.4 KB, so the two or three index inserts a datom needs are ~3-4k ticks and ~4 KB;
- a fresh :memory db without history, maps with tempids: 13.2k ticks, 23 KB;
- explicit entity ids as [:db/add e a v]: 10.4k ticks, 15 KB;
- with history (test-db): 14.9k ticks, 25.8 KB;
- a :db/unique identity attribute: x1.6 (23k, 58 KB);
- a content-id identity (:var/name): x2.8 (41k, 132 KB per datom).
So ~7k ticks and ~11 KB of each plain datom are the add path around the inserts (datahike.db.transaction: transact-add, with-datom's validate-datom, attr-info, the cond-> of update-in on the db record, hash, op-count), and identities and content ids multiply it. Estimate: a datom costs its index inserts plus a few hundred ticks, ~4-5k ticks; the import ~0.35 s, not 5.4 s. Cause: not found. Jolt has no profiler for uncontracted code, so the next step is to time the add path's parts at the REPL (attr-info, validate-datom, the record updates, the cardinality-one search, content-tempids), largest first, and fix the largest at its cause on a jolt/<topic> Datahike branch. Proofs: a cost proof of d/db-with of n plain datoms at 1,000 and 10,000, per datom within 2x of the index inserts, and one with :db/unique and content-id identities."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.db-test/a-datom-costs-its-index-inserts}}]
